## 2. 20-Module Enterprise Argo CD Curriculum Deep Dive

---

### Module 1: GitOps Operating Model & Argo CD Control Plane Architecture (Page 1)

```
                            ARGO CD ARCHITECTURE
                               [ Git Repository ]
                            (Single Source of Truth)
                                       │ (HTTPS / SSH Poll & Webhook)
                                       ▼
 ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │                         ARGO CD CONTROL PLANE                               │
 │                                                                             │
 │  ┌─────────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────────┐     ┌───────────────┐  │
 │  │ API Server          │     │ Repository Server   │     │ Dex (OIDC/SSO)│  │
 │  │ (REST, gRPC, Web UI)│     │ (Clones Git/Renders)│     │ Auth Provider │  │
 │  └──────────┬──────────┘     └──────────┬──────────┘     └───────────────┘  │
 │             │                           │                                   │
 │             ▼                           ▼                                   │
 │  ┌─────────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────────┐     ┌───────────────┐  │
 │  │ Redis Cache         │     │ Application         │     │ Notifications │  │
 │  │ (State & Rate Limit)│     │ Controller (Reconc) │     │ Controller    │  │
 │  └─────────────────────┘     └──────────┬──────────┘     └───────────────┘  │
 └─────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┘
                                           │ (K8s API Reconciliation)
                                           ▼
                            [ Target Kubernetes Cluster ]
                            (Actual Live Running State)
```

#### 🔄 GitOps vs. Traditional Push-Based CI/CD
| Feature | Traditional Push CI/CD (Jenkins, GitLab CI) | Modern GitOps (Argo CD Pull Model) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Execution Point** | External runner pushes commands via `kubectl` | Internal agent pulls manifests inside cluster |
| **Security Exposure**| Requires storing high-privilege cluster tokens in CI | Zero cluster credentials exposed to external CI |
| **Drift Detection** | None (Runs once on commit; blind to cluster drift) | Continuous loop (Alerts/reverts drift in seconds) |
| **Auditability** | Scatted across build logs and pipeline histories | Git commit log is the definitive audit trail |
| **Rollback Model** | Re-run old pipeline (Slow, imperative, error-prone)| `git revert` commit (Instant, declarative, safe) |

