### Module 14: Multi-Cluster Management & Credential Secret Topologies (Page 14)

```bash
# Register an external EKS cluster into Argo CD
argocd cluster add <kubecontext-name> \
  --name prod-us-east-cluster \
  --label env=production \
  --label region=us-east-1
```

```yaml
# Under the hood, Argo CD stores cluster credentials in an encrypted secret:
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: cluster-prod-us-east
  namespace: argocd
  labels:
    argocd.argoproj.io/secret-type: cluster
type: Opaque
stringData:
  name: prod-us-east-cluster
  server: https://123456789.gr7.us-east-1.eks.amazonaws.com
  config: |
    {
      "bearerToken": "<short-lived-sa-token>",
      "tlsClientConfig": {
        "insecure": false,
        "caData": "<base64-ca-cert>"
      }
    }
```

